{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Landing status — patch set 3 on change 1488, awaiting CI\n\n**https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1488**\n\n- **PS1** earned **LLM-Review +1** (\"PASS, 1 advisory finding, non-blocking\", no inline\n  comments) and **Verified +1** — the FULL CI matrix green on ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and\n  macos py3.13, plus every drift/optionality/identity gate.\n- **Submit was refused with a 409**: Gerrit could not auto-rebase because change 1487 (ticket\n  4bf4) landed first and touches the same file. This is the exact conflict predicted and\n  pre-resolved in the comment above, so it was expected, not a surprise.\n- **PS2** = rebased onto 4bf4, conflict resolved keep-both. That resolution left ONE blank\n  line where ruff wants two, and CI's lint job caught it — my error: I re-ran the tests after\n  resolving but not `make lint`. PS2 is superseded.\n- **PS3** = PS2 + `ruff format`. Locally on the exact PS3 tree: `make lint` clean,\n  `make typecheck` clean (436 files), and the jscpd + lizard suites 13/13 green INCLUDING\n  both integration tests. Independently, the wider targeted run was 1643 passed / 11 skipped,\n  no regressions.\n\nPS3's CI (run 31174513500) has been QUEUED for ~1 hour without starting — GitHub Actions\nrunner capacity is saturated by the many changes other agents are pushing concurrently. That\nis an infrastructure wait, not a signal about this change: PS3 differs from the already-\nVerified PS1 only by the rebase onto 4bf4 and one whitespace character.\n\n**Ticket deliberately left `in_progress`, NOT closed** — per AGENTS.md a ticket must not close\nuntil its change is `Verified +1` and merged, and a passing completion-verifier is not a\nsubstitute for green CI. The worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/6067-lizard-zero` is retained (branch\n`6067-lizard-zero`, commit `fa58a320d5`) since the fix has not landed.\n\n**To finish:** wait for PS3's `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`, Submit, then\n`rebar transition 6067 in_progress closed`. No code work remains."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786102667324681001,"uuid":"6b65b8f2-5809-478b-bc40-505a3c8bd520"}